                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[quote][url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/7871885/]Follow our curator page:[b] OCG-Curations[/b] if you like and want to see more reviews like this one.[/url][/quote]\n\n[h1]Wobbly Jungle - Review[/h1]\n\n[b]Gameplay:[/b]\nWhen I first looked at this game I didn't expect much from it. Looked like a very basic, simple platformer. And whilst it isn't revolutionizing the genre, it certainly did a very good job at offering challenging, long lasting and varying gameplay.\nThe controls are very basic - move and jump - with the addition of double jumps and wall jumps.\nWhilst the game seemed to be quite simple at the first few levels, I soon was faced with a repertory of crazy and challenging\ntwists - forcing me to act both fast, and cleverly.\nThe game offers 60 levels, which come with lots of hours of diverse adventure.\nThe only real problem I encountered whilst ingame, was the camera management - often you don't see where you need to jump and you're just forced to leap and hope for the best.\nThus, the gameplay overall is solid, what is missing are some other things: \nThe menus are very confusing and lack some features (for instance the ability to manage the volume!), and the game comes\nwith only one track, which repeats every 3 minutes.\nFurthermore, great potential was given up, by leaving out the ability to create own levels and share those.\n\n[b]Pros:[/b]\n+High variety in gameplay\n+A lot of content\n+Challenging \n+Simple controls\n\n[b]Cons:[/b]\n-Poor menu management\n-Soundtrack consists of one track\n\n[b]Conclusion:[/b]\nAlltogether I can praise this game for both its length and challenge and can only recommend it.\n[u]8.5/10[/u]",
